Hi,

I'd like to report a bug in the hid-playstation driver affecting the Sony
DualSense Edge Wireless Controller (054C:0DF2) when connected via Bluetooth=
.


## Summary

The DualSense Edge sends a trailing null byte (0x00) at the end of its HID
report descriptor over Bluetooth. The hid-playstation driver does not
handle this gracefully, logs "unknown main item tag 0x0", and falls back to
registering the device as a generic "DualSense controller" rather than a
"DualSense Edge controller". This causes Edge-specific features to be
unavailable and results in incorrect output report formatting over
Bluetooth, which triggers link tx timeout and connection drops when any
output report (LED/lightbar, haptics) is sent to the device.

The same device connected via USB does NOT have the trailing null byte and
works correctly.


## Hardware

- Controller: Sony DualSense Edge Wireless Controller (VID: 054C, PID: 0DF2=
)
- Bluetooth Adapter: Foxconn / Hon Hai (0489:e10a) =E2=80=94 MediaTek MT792=
5 (MSI
B850 Gaming Plus WiFi)
- HCI Version: 5.3


## Software

- OS: Nobara Linux 43 (based on Fedora 43)
- Kernel: 7.0.5-200.nobara.fc43.x86_64
- BlueZ: 5.84
- Driver: hid-playstation (author: Sony Interactive Entertainment,
srcversion: B0C2D9A799115DCE2664703)


## Steps to Reproduce

1. Pair a DualSense Edge controller to a Linux system via Bluetooth
2. Connect the controller
3. Observe dmesg output
4. Attempt to send any output report (e.g. change LED color via Steam or
dualsensectl)


## Actual Behavior

dmesg on connect:

  playstation 0005:054C:0DF2.000A: unknown main item tag 0x0
  playstation 0005:054C:0DF2.000A: hidraw7: BLUETOOTH HID v1.00 Gamepad
[DualSense Edge Wireless Controller] on ec:91:61:d0:5d:a6
  input: DualSense Edge Wireless Controller as
/devices/virtual/misc/uhid/0005:054C:0DF2.000A/input/input29
  input: DualSense Edge Wireless Controller Motion Sensors as
/devices/virtual/misc/uhid/0005:054C:0DF2.000A/input/input30
  input: DualSense Edge Wireless Controller Touchpad as
/devices/virtual/misc/uhid/0005:054C:0DF2.000A/input/input31
  playstation 0005:054C:0DF2.000A: Registered DualSense controller
hw_version=3D0x01000223 fw_version=3D0x0100008b

Note: final line says "DualSense controller" not "DualSense Edge
controller".

dmesg when any output report is sent:

  Bluetooth: hci0: link tx timeout
  Bluetooth: hci0: killing stalled connection d4:2f:4b:3d:ec:a6
  Bluetooth: hci0: link tx timeout
  Bluetooth: hci0: killing stalled connection d4:2f:4b:3d:ec:a6


## Root Cause

The Bluetooth HID report descriptor ends with:

  ... b1 02 85 f7 09 2f 95 07 b1 02 c0 00

c0 is the valid HID End Collection tag. The trailing 00 is an invalid null
byte with no corresponding HID item tag, which the driver flags as "unknown
main item tag 0x0".

The USB descriptor ends cleanly:

  ... b1 02 85 7b 09 53 b1 02 c0

No trailing null byte, no parse error, device works correctly.

The Bluetooth and USB descriptors also differ significantly in structure:
- USB: 6 analog axes (X, Y, Z, Rz, Rx, Ry), 15 buttons
- Bluetooth: 4 analog axes (X, Y, Z, Rz only), 14 buttons, different vendor
report IDs

The driver falls back to generic DualSense handling when it cannot fully
parse the Edge Bluetooth descriptor, resulting in incorrect output report
formatting that the controller rejects.


## Suggested Fix

1. Tolerate trailing null bytes in the HID report descriptor =E2=80=94 a nu=
ll byte
after the closing c0 End Collection tag is harmless and should be ignored
or stripped before parsing.

2. Correctly identify the DualSense Edge over Bluetooth using PID 0x0DF2
regardless of descriptor parse warnings, rather than falling back to
generic DualSense handling.

3. Use the correct Bluetooth-specific output report format for the
DualSense Edge, as the Bluetooth descriptor layout differs significantly
from the USB descriptor layout.


## Additional Notes

- Controller firmware is current (verified via PS5 console, version 0217)
- Issue does not occur over USB =E2=80=94 full functionality including LED/=
lightbar
control works correctly
- UserspaceHID=3Dtrue in /etc/bluetooth/input.conf partially mitigates outp=
ut
report instability but does not resolve the descriptor parse error or
incorrect device registration
- UserspaceHID=3Dfalse (kernel HIDP) causes output reports over Bluetooth t=
o
immediately trigger link tx timeout

I have attached the full HID report descriptors from /sys/kernel/debug/hid/
for both USB and Bluetooth connections.

Thanks for looking into this.

Caleb

